  "statSections": [
    {
      "name": "Traits",
      "rulesText": "Stench. Constitution Saving Throw: DC 10, any creature that starts its turn in a 5-foot Emanation originating from the ghast. Failure: The target has the Poisoned condition until the start of its next turn. Success: The target is immune to this ghast's Stench for 24 hours.",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "Monsters A-Z",
        "section": "12.97",
        "heading": "Traits",
        "lineStart": 20902,
        "lineEnd": 20904
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Actions",
      "rulesText": "Bite. Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 7 (1d8 + 3) Piercing damage plus 9 (2d8) Necrotic damage.\n\nClaw. Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6 + 3) Slashing damage. If the target is a non-Undead creature, it is subjected to the following effect. Constitution Saving Throw: DC 10. Failure: The target has the Paralyzed condition until the end of its next turn.",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "Monsters A-Z",
        "section": "12.97",
        "heading": "Actions",
        "lineStart": 20906,
        "lineEnd": 20910
      }
    }
  ],
  "rulesText": "Medium Undead, Chaotic Evil\n\nAC 13\nInitiative +3 (13)\nHP 36 (8d8)\nSpeed 30 ft.\n\nResistances Necrotic\nImmunities Poison; Charmed, Exhaustion, Poisoned\nSenses Darkvision 60 ft.; Passive Perception 10\nLanguages Common\nCR 2 (XP 450; PB +2)\n\nTraits\n\nStench. Constitution Saving Throw: DC 10, any creature that starts its turn in a 5-foot Emanation originating from the ghast. Failure: The target has the Poisoned condition until the start of its next turn. Success: The target is immune to this ghast's Stench for 24 hours.\n\nActions\n\nBite. Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 7 (1d8 + 3) Piercing damage plus 9 (2d8) Necrotic damage.\n\nClaw. Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6 + 3) Slashing damage. If the target is a non-Undead creature, it is subjected to the following effect. Constitution Saving Throw: DC 10. Failure: The target has the Paralyzed condition until the end of its next turn.",
